WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Two poem shapes on a page:
a block of fourteen lines,

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.870
and three short stanzas of five.

3
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.120
Above them, a label: GCSE.

4
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:12.540
You know this task.

5
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.960
Read the poem, find the
methods, explain them.

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.300
Then the label peels away.

7
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.580
Underneath: A-level.

8
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.150
The page hasn't changed.

9
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.960
Same kind of task, a different ask.

10
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.040
So what does A-level
want that GCSE didn't?

11
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:35.240
In this mission, you'll set what GCSE
often rewards beside what A-level adds.

12
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.660
You'll read two unseen poems,
each about a partner leaving.

13
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.220
And you'll ask what a
poem's shape is doing:

14
00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.610
where it turns, and why.

15
00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:50.690
Your mission: find out what A-level wants
from an unseen poem that GCSE didn't.
